Description: use another computer's desktop with your USB devices and folders
 PairDesk connects Linux computers on your network: full remote desktop
 with clipboard, sound and microphone, plus USB device sharing in both
 directions (security keys such as YubiKey, webcams, USB drives), and
 shared folders in both directions.
 .
 One package on every computer; a switch turns remote access on or off.
 Connections use PairDesk's own encrypted link service: it runs as the
 user on its own port (default 4722), is open only while remote access is
 on, accepts only computers paired with a one-time code, and carries the
 desktop, USB devices and folders over one connection.
 .
 Only Python, GTK and the SSH client are required. The viewer, folder
 sharing, SSH server, USB sharing and other add-ons are installed when first
 needed, after PairDesk explains what they are for; pairdesk-uninstall
 removes them again.
